{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZInputs","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZInputs","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZIdentification"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.cluster_residue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.cluster_residue","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LagrangianKZInputs.lean#L209-L277","doc":"**Residue of a colliding cluster.** For symmetric residues, distinct positions `w` inside the\ncluster and `ε ≠ 0`, the form along the collision direction is `ε⁻¹` times half the sum of the\ncluster's pair residues, plus a term that stays regular as `ε → 0` whenever `c` differs from\nevery outside point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.clusterDir","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.clusterDir","kind":"def","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LagrangianKZInputs.lean#L205-L207","doc":"The collision direction: `w` on the cluster, `0` outside. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.clusterConfig","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.clusterConfig","kind":"def","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LagrangianKZInputs.lean#L201-L203","doc":"The configuration where the cluster `S` sits at `c + ε w` and the others stay at `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.affineInvariant_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.affineInvariant_iff","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LagrangianKZInputs.lean#L168-L182","doc":"**Invariance is factoring through the normal form.** A function on configurations with\n`z_0 ≠ z_1` is invariant under all dilations and translations iff it only depends on\n`affineNormalize z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.affineNormalize_eq_affine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.affineNormalize_eq_affine","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LagrangianKZInputs.lean#L160-L166","doc":"On configurations with `z_0 ≠ z_1`, the normal form is reached by an affine map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.affineNormalize_affine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.affineNormalize_affine","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LagrangianKZInputs.lean#L151-L158","doc":"The normal form is invariant under every dilation `c ≠ 0` and every translation `b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.affineNormalize","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.affineNormalize","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LagrangianKZInputs.lean#L147-L149","doc":"Affine normal form of a configuration: move `z_0` to `0` and `z_1` to `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.arnoldForm_eq_abelian_add_kz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.arnoldForm_eq_abelian_add_kz","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LagrangianKZInputs.lean#L127-L139","doc":"**The form, assembled.** Equivariance plus one Schur–Weyl pair residue writes the whole\nArnold-class form as an abelian part plus the KZ form with `ℏ = β` and `Ω_{ij} = P_{(ij)}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.residue_uniform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.residue_uniform","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LagrangianKZInputs.lean#L113-L125","doc":"**One pair fixes all pairs.** With covariant residues, if one pair residue is\n`α + β P_{(i₀ j₀)}`, then every pair residue is `α + β P_{(ij)}` with the same `α, β`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.exists_perm_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.exists_perm_pair","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LagrangianKZInputs.lean#L100-L111","doc":"A permutation sending a given ordered pair of distinct labels to another. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.swap_covariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.swap_covariant","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LagrangianKZInputs.lean#L94-L98","doc":"The strand-transposition residues are covariant: `g_σ P_{(ij)} g_σ⁻¹ = P_{(σi σj)}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.residue_covariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.residue_covariant","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LagrangianKZInputs.lean#L84-L92","doc":"**Equivariance forces covariant residues.** If relabelling the points by `σ` acts on the form\nby conjugation with `g σ`, then `M_{σa,σb} = g_σ M_{ab} g_σ⁻¹` for every `a ≠ b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.arnoldForm_relabel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.LagrangianKZ.arnoldForm_relabel","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/LagrangianKZInputs.lean#L74-L82","doc":"**Relabelling.** Moving the point labelled `a` to label `σ a` (`(σ·z)_{σ a} = z_a`) turns the\nArnold-class form with residues `M` into the one with residues `M_{σa,σb}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}